      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Annular pancreas divisum is a rare congenital variant of pancreatic anatomy which may cause symptoms of gastric outlet obstruction and recurrent pancreatitis. It is diagnosed by endoscopic retrograde pancreatography. We present two cases of this condition and review the literature."},
